# topo-fanout-fanin-declared-order-variant — the same policy as
# topo-fanout-fanin-declared-order (A fans out to B and C; both fan in to D;
# B and C are mutually incomparable in the pipe relation), but C is declared
# before B. The declaration-order tie-break (SPEC §7.4) therefore fixes a
# different log: A, C, B, D. Same graph shape, same per-gate verdicts and
# master decision as the sibling vector; only the evaluation order — and so
# the log — differs, exactly as the declaration-order rule requires.
actor a
gate  A grant a
gate  C
gate  B grant a
gate  D grant a
cord a -> A
cord A -> B
cord A -> C
cord B -> D
cord C -> D
cord D -> master
